From 8d54d1328cc9aa8857486cbb6f4b8fac6ab7a8a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:13:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web-scan): keep recheck state through reorg stops; never
 skip blocks below a window reorg (pre-existing)

H1 (introduced by the recheck design): the reorg stop paths of runScan (the
announcement limit, the match limit, a provider disagreement, an open-lane
deferral, and an anchor the second provider does not corroborate after a
reorg) called checkpoints.clear(). That deleted the persisted rescanFrom and
the recheck list, pending-owed blocks included, so the overflow notice
vanished without a save. Each path now saves an anchor-less checkpoint
{ nextBlock: lo } (reorgStopCheckpoint) instead. It carries the owed blocks
below lo: the stored list (the incoming cursor's, or this run's last save),
this run's pending and main-scan recheck matches, and the rescan block when
it is below lo. They are capped and counted by withOwedRechecks itself. No
anchor is persisted, so the fail-closed intent of the clear is kept: no
orphaned anchor can be treated as canonical on resume. An overflow found by
such a save is reported on that progress and on the result.

H2 (pre-existing on the integration base 4a38efd, in the same lines): a
window-end reorg reports rolledBackTo = w.from of a later window, above the
page start. The limit, deferral and disagreement stops set the cursor there,
so announcements in [page start, w.from) were never processed and were
skipped for good, with any genuine payment in them. Every reorg stop now
holds the in-memory cursor and the save at lo = min(rolledBackTo, page
start). Both provider comparisons of a reorg page also start at lo.

M1/M2/L2: pin the pending-owed bound (a pending match at or after the saved
nextBlock is not owed; a lower owed block keeps its retry after a reload),
the typed-start rescanFrom carry in the view, and the carried < nextBlock
guard.

L1: while the rescan block an earlier session handed this run is still owed,
the overflow is marked countKnown: false and the view shows the
count-neutral scan.recheck.overflowSaved copy. A reorg stop that carries
this run's own rescan block keeps the count known.

L3: document that a pending recheck below the run start pins saves to the
run start while it stays pending (fail closed; spam cannot cause it).

